        "original_id": "0fd08c14-50a2-55ce-a988-4faf74e30729",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Porsche 911, Porsche 997, Porsche 993, Carrera 4, Carrera 4S, Targa 911, Type 964, Type 991\n- Concepts: Targa body style, glass canopy roof design\n\nFacts:\n- The Porsche 993 was Porsche's internal name for a Porsche 911 version manufactured and sold from late 1993 to early 1998.\n- In the United States, the Porsche 993 corresponded to model years 1995 through 1998.\n- The Porsche 993 replaced the Type 964.\n- Targa versions of the Porsche 997 Carrera 4 and Carrera 4S were available in addition to coupé and cabriolet versions.\n- The Porsche 997 Targa versions continued the glass canopy roof design used on all Targa 911 models from the Type 993 generation through the Type 991.\n- The Type 991 replaced that glass canopy roof design in 2012.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e204cc1c-3757-56e2-9849-56835928fe64",
        "text": "Page: Porsche 997. Sentence: In addition to the coupé and cabriolet versions, Targa versions of the Carrera 4 and Carrera 4S were also available, which carry on with the \"glass canopy\" roof design used on all Targa 911s from the Type 993 Generation 911 until the 991, which replaced it in 2012.\nPage: Porsche 993. Sentence: 993 is the company's internal name for the version of the Porsche 911 model manufactured and sold between late 1993 and early 1998 (model years 1995-1998 in the United States), replacing the 964.",
